  "title": "Video found its way into the workflow",
  "summary": "Video became easier to make, media models gained clearer choices, and the routes into generation got shorter.\n\nPreview MP4 generation arrived for Veo 3.1 Fast and Seedance, then chat added `/video`, model selection, and in-conversation playback. Seedance also gained image-to-video handling and, by week’s end, two explicit choices: `seedance` for Lite and `seedance-pro` for Pro-Fast.\n\nThe final Seedream split makes `seedream` the 4.0 choice and `seedream-pro` the 4.5 choice, with 4K and multi-image support. Media request fixes improved handling of small images and reference images with generic file types. GPT Image edits now keep img2img requests on `gpt-image-1-mini`.\n\nThe new `gen.pollinations.ai` gateway adds shorter image and text routes, OpenAI-compatible requests, and a `/models` shortcut. The docs now use those paths and explain text query parameters. `nova-micro` joined the text models for conversations and tool use.\n\nSession-level system prompts and generation settings, charts in messages, and collapsible streamed reasoning give chat more room for actual work. Request changes also keep model-specific thinking settings from being sent where they do not belong.",
